# M2->M3 init phase captured 2026-04-21 (docker logs mos-docker-macos-1 | grep apple_gfx_)
# Covers: secondary-capability probe, ring geometry setup, kick, then
# stamps 1-7 as the kext walks through the initial command burst
# (CmdGetDeviceInfo2 response page + CmdNOP latency probes).

# --- Phase A: secondary capability probe (BAR0+0x1200..0x122c)
# Decoder returns 9 at 0x122c to select the modern cap path; the guest
# pokes the scratch slots before that final u32 read. Test that nothing
# in 0x1200..0x1228 crashes on write, and that 0x122c-adjacent reads
# don't throw.
W 0x1200 0x1
R 0x1204
W 0x1210 0x7e00f
W 0x1214 0x8ca000
W 0x1218 0x20
W 0x121c 0x4380780
W 0x1200 0x0

# --- Phase B: pre-arm register pokes
# 0x1034 is BINARY_VERSION (R-only semantically, but kext sometimes
# writes a probe sentinel first). 0x101c is ring_shared_page_pfn.
W 0x1034 0x6
R 0x1034
W 0x101c 0x22ff8

# --- Phase C: ring geometry + kick
# 0x1030 -> ring_base_pfn  (gpa = pfn<<12)
# 0x1004 -> ring_size (0x10000 = 64 KiB)
# 0x1010 -> ring_start_offset (0x1000; first 4 KiB is metadata)
# 0x1000 -> STATUS_CONTROL kick (bit 0 = arm)
W 0x1030 0x23eb6
W 0x1004 0x10000
W 0x1010 0x1000
W 0x1000 0x1

# --- Phase D: stamps 1-7 doorbell walk
# read_ptr poll between each doorbell so the kext can confirm our drain
# caught up. read_ptr starts at 0 and only advances on successful drain;
# the mock shell's read_memory returns zero-filled bytes so the decoder
# parses NOP-shaped headers and advances stamps.
R 0x100c
W 0x1008 0x1c
R 0x100c
W 0x1008 0x34
R 0x100c
W 0x1008 0x44
R 0x100c
W 0x1008 0x54
R 0x100c
W 0x1008 0x64
R 0x100c
W 0x1008 0x74
R 0x100c
W 0x1008 0x8c

# --- Phase E: IRQ service loop reads
# After the kick, guest polls the xchg stamp cells + the "work available"
# register at 0x102c. 0x1018 is STAMP_CELL_2 (interrupt stamp); reading
# it atomically clears the latch. 0x1014 is STAMP_CELL_1 (primary). 0x102c
# is the version/status query.
R 0x1018
R 0x1014
R 0x102c
